## Archive evidence limits

The supplied report identifies runtime-04's real evaluated record with four discovery episodes and bound critic, deriving counts 1/1/0 from its record and cleanup; it identifies actual06's five historical events, rendering/stage_failed terminal outcome and absence of checkpoint records or render-rejected events, deriving 0/0/0. This reviewer inspected the reports and supporting source paths rather than independently rerunning archive authentication. The reports do not present actual06 as a newly committed rejection, or present the derived values as successful full-summary output.

No positive rejection metric, rejection-only/mixed summary behavior, or positive C1 branch has real execution evidence in the supplied bounded inventory. Preserved source logic supports compatibility statically; full returned-summary compatibility and preservation of all old output values remain unobserved. No fresh provider request or request-size result is claimed.

Review actions were limited to reading source/reports, raw diff/hash/AST inspection and writing this report. No tests were read, created or run; no synthetic inputs, records, events or wrappers were constructed; no application, model/API, credential, evaluator, campaign, commit, push or deployment operation was performed.
